Implement Technical Controls and Evidence Capture
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Deploy and configure auditd, fail2ban, and AIDE as technical controls on Ubuntu
Implement access control (AC-2, AC-3) and audit logging (AU-2, AU-12) settings
Validate configuration baselines using OpenSCAP
Capture and hash evidence artifacts in a tamper-evident structure
Build an evidence index mapping artifacts to SP 800-53 control IDs
Prerequisites
Basic Linux command line skills (users, permissions, systemd)
Familiarity with SP 800-53 control families (AC, AU)
Understanding of CGRC Domains 4 (Implementation) and 5 (Assessment)
Comfort editing config files with nano or vim
Environment Setup
Al Nafi provides a single Ubuntu Linux machine via Start Lab
Log in via the provided terminal/SSH access
Update the system before starting:
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
Task 1: Deploy Hardened Workload Components
Install the core control tools:

sudo apt install -y auditd audispd-plugins fail2ban aide aide-common
Verify each service:

sudo systemctl status auditd --no-pager
sudo systemctl status fail2ban --no-pager
Initialize AIDE (file integrity baseline):

sudo aideinit
